+MyoConverter supplies the initial OpenSim-to-MuJoCo translation. I added procedures for repairing custom muscle paths and checking joint conventions, then coupled the converted model to an SNS-Toolbox controller. The converted model carries 92 muscle-tendon actuators. Comparing attachment paths with the OpenSim source checks the transferred geometry; activating individual actuators checks the direction of the resulting joint torque. These checks concern conversion fidelity, not the ability of the controller to produce walking. The neural and mechanical models exchange signals at a \qty{2}{\milli\second} step.
 
